<title>USA: Balanced budget amendment may fail in Senate - Rubin.</title>
<headline>Balanced budget amendment may fail in Senate - Rubin.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate looks likely to fall short of the two-thirds vote needed for passage of a balanced budget amendment to the Constitution, Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks as if there is a good chance it will not be successful in the Senate,&quot; Rubin told a group of secondary school students here.</p>
<p>The Senate is expected to vote on the amendemnt on Tuesday. The administration is opposed to it.</p>
</text>
